  "notes": "CHILL quadrant — smallest with 5 countries, but two standout stories. (1) SWE: $59,058 is only $142 below the $59,200 mean — it's CHILL by a rounding error. Its $41.01/hr matches AUS ($41.44) and CAN ($41.15) in GRIND who work hundreds more hours. Annotation badge emphasizes the near-miss. (2) JPN: the karoshi paradox — Japan is culturally synonymous with overwork but OECD data puts it below average hours because OECD counts ALL workers including Japan's massive part-time workforce. The '?' icon and karoshi overlay draw attention to this statistical nuance. Script is careful: 'The statistic is accurate — it just measures something different than most people expect.' No connector lines needed — the annotations tell both stories. Math verified: SWE $59,058 = $59,200 - $142. JPN hourly: $49,446/1,607 = $30.77."
